Summary: Dancing in circles...

I've noticed monsters, particularly my pet, behaving very oddly on a number of
occasions.  Once that I recall, I couldn't seem to convince my pet to go
through a particular door without using tripe rations as a 'persuader'; I
didn't think much of it, until it happened again.  This time, the dog wouldn't
leave the southern portion of a particular room.  If there were one of those
doorless closets with a scroll of teleport inside, might the dog be trying to
get at the item to pick it up?  (I finally out-prioritied it by dropping tripe
just outside a room, and standing on it (so as not to lose the tripe); the dog
trotted over, and I picked up the meat and left.

On a possibly related note, my Tourist was hurting after a series of
encounters with a hobbit, a kobold, and one other critter, none of which I'd
been able to finish off.  I retreated to the corner of a room to rest up, and
the three of them showed up again... and proceeded to go in circles, entering
the room through one door, milling about a bit, then getting pushed out
another room by the next monster in line.  Naturally, throwing darts got
their attention, but since they gave me time to rest, I polished them off
without trouble.  So why in the world were they doing that?

Oh, one last thing: I had an identify spell, costing 5 energy points.  I was
at 6 for 6, so tried casting it.  I was told that I didn't have enough energy;
I wasn't hungry, but I was somewhat burdened.  What happened?

